WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.300
Now, let's begin.

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:08.230
I've been waiting 70 years for this moment!

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.190
This is the moment I crush you!

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.200
Watase Aoba!

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:19.160
Aoba!

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.210
Found you, traitor!

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.790
Wait, Tarjim!

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.340
Die!

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:32.920
Damn it!

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:34.970
Go!

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:35.970
Hurry!

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:48.440
Damn, he's fast...

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.790
If only...

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:53.320
If only you had never appeared, I would have...

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:57.490
He's gone?

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.790
Become a lump of flesh and die!

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.070
Spread your wings

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:17.700
See the light of hope in the sky you have yet to witness

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.990
And don't ever give in to the weight of sorrow

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:26.370
Echo unto eternity, "Unisonia"

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:35.630
That world you see before your eyes

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:41.220
I wonder what colors it is made of

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.680
The pain of loss isn't something

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:48.650
You want to get used to, and yet

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:53.610
Even on a night like this, the stars glisten

00:01:54.610 --> 00:02:00.570
Like a tarnished coin spilling from the palm of your hand

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.410
Can't go back

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:03.830
Want to go home

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:07.160
The two of them back-to-back

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.210
Break through

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:13.960
Turning unfading emotions into a lasting bond

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:17.300
Like painting over a colorless world

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.010
Let this sympathy reach

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:26.270
Let's build the future that we envision

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:29.480
You'll see, we'll even change fate

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:34.280
Transcending time, "Unisonia"

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.810
You squirrelly little...

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:52.940
What in the world is this Valiancer?!

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.980
It's performing like a Coupling Machine all by itself.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:58.170
It isn't a Coupling Machine?

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:01.660
That's impossible. Without a Buddy Valiancer...

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.660
Could it be...

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:04.950
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:10.750
<i>But then, that would explain the system
interference and the forced Decoupling...</i>

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.710
Do you have some sort of a plan?

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.170
It's not based on anything conclusive, but...

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.300
Give it a try anyway.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:22.550
Either way, if we can't use the Coupling Machines, we don't stand a chance of winning.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.050
I understand.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.470
Mayu, lend me a hand.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:26.390
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:34.730
You've got some nerve showing up here!

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.230
This is for Bizon!

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.740
Wait, Tarjim! Let's hear what Hina has to say!

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.200
Shut up!

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.250
Damn it! I can't hit him!

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.340
Aoba!

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:59.300
Damn!

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.050
Dio, we need to perform a Coupling!

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:01.920
What?!

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.930
There's no other way to fight that bastard!

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.850
But, Elvira-san said we're being jammed!

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.490
We don't know if it's impossible unless we try!

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:11.100
Got it.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.060
Here goes!

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.310
Connect with Dio!

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:14.560
Accept!

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.620
Don't you understand that it's futile?! You fools!

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.450
What?!

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.420
What was that? His movement suddenly got...

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:37.330
I don't know.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:38.340
But this is our chance!

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.960
What's going on?

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:44.720
Oh, it seems you've reached the time limit.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.640
Start it back up again immediately.

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.550
Do not set a time limit.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:51.560
But without it, your brain will...

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.730
I have no use for your excuses!

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:55.060
Oh, all right.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:58.060
Honestly, you don't get it, do you?

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:04.820
Even if the System is first-rate, with a second-rate part it won't live up to its fullest potential.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.530
And by "part", I mean you the pilot.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:19.130
Here I come, Watase Aoba!

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:22.160
Damn it, here he comes again!

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:23.010
Damn.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.300
Is this really possible?

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.180
There's no doubt about it.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.680
But is such a thing even achievable?

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:34.890
Even with the current cockpits, if we load the system into them, it's theoretically possible.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:37.020
It'll be a real high-wire act...

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:41.520
But it would also explain how we're being jammed.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:45.490
We may have a shot at making the plan I showed you earlier a reality.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:50.020
Captain.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:53.410
How long until the system can be implemented?

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:54.830
Just say the word.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:58.870
I understand.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:01.040
It doesn't look like we have any other choice.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.040
Make it happen.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:02.920
Yes, sir.

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:03.550
Mayu.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:04.550
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:07.130
This...

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.470
Am I to believe that it is righteous to fight like this?

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:14.180
Commander.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:20.190
We've finished installing the system.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:22.110
We'll instruct you with regards to the timing.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.940
But is such a thing...

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.230
It's possible.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:26.820
The XO asked the same thing.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:30.200
Besides, look. Here comes the princess.

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:32.530
Aoba!

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:33.740
Is that you, Hina?!

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:40.210
Sorry about that.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:43.540
I've been instructed by my captain to back her up.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.880
Damn. They're all getting on my nerves!

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:47.970
Let's do this, Dio!

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:48.970
But...

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:53.100
You're going to say something about how we haven't tried it yet, aren't you?

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.010
You know it.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.060
Don't screw this up.

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:56.850
I won't!

00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:00.600
You sit tight there, Hina!

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:04.230
I'll spend plenty of time playing with you once I've killed Aoba.

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:06.980
You won't get away.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:14.450
Activating Stand Alone Mode!

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:15.330
Now!

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:17.330
Connect with Luxon!

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.340
What?!

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:37.470
What the hell?!

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:41.390
We created an artificial persona within the Coupling Machine's System...

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:46.520
By establishing a virtual link with the unit, it is possible to conduct a solo Coupling.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:49.400
They were able to build it in such a short amount of time?!

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.780
We just threw this together, and we're not using it as it was primarily intended.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:54.780
Plus, it puts a huge strain on the pilot,

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:57.450
so we'll only be able to use it for just a short while, but...

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:05.040
In a Coupling, synching the thoughts of the two pilots

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:09.710
requires sending elementary particles as thought data one nanosecond into the future.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.670
In a solo Coupling

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:15.680
it's like you're linking up with yourself,
so there's no need to receive that data.

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:18.810
So then, what happens to the leftover outgoing data?

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:24.520
The reception of that outgoing data is interpreted as interference which disrupts the Coupling System.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.940
That's what was behind the jamming.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:32.900
Not so fast!

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:36.450
You may have been able to build the system, but as for the Valiancer's performance...

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:42.370
If we can emit the same interference, we can cancel out the jamming!

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:43.330
You two!

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:44.040
Yes, ma'am!

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:44.640
All right!

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:47.500
Disengaging Stand Alone Mode!

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.250
Connect with Aoba!
Connect with Aoba!

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:50.750
Accept!

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:09.820
Impossible!

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:11.280
Impossible! Impossible!

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:14.360
Th-This doesn't mean that I am inferior to Elvira!

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:17.950
That's right. If I only had the same parts that she has...

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:20.660
Those superior parts!

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:23.370
Perform a Coupling with three people?

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:24.450
Yes, sir.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:29.460
Aoba and Hina Ryazan's Emphater Waveforms were completely identical.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:34.380
In terms of the System, this makes it possible to be identified as one individual.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:38.050
If we could then have Dio perform a Coupling...

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:39.140
What would happen?

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:41.510
This is unknown territory.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:43.270
We won't know until we try...

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.350
I am being swallowed up...

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:50.770
My thought data...

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:56.150
Stop...

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:08.010
Take this fleeting, crimson pain...

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:09.320
These are...

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:13.050
Take this fleeting, crimson pain...
Take this fleeting, crimson pain...

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:13.460
Hina's memories?

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:19.380
and set it adrift under this sky
and set it adrift under this sky

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:25.390
One, then another, they vanish
One, then another, they vanish

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:32.440
The fire of life burns
The fire of life burns

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:38.360
Amidst these many thousands of stars, I met you
Amidst these many thousands of stars, I met you

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.740
In the first Coupling experiment, Hina alone got sent through.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:46.040
With these shared thoughts in my heart, I can fly
With these shared thoughts in my heart, I can fly

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:49.120
Rise up, O nameless warrior

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.960
Spark a light of hope in your heart

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.310
As long as you can ignite the will to fight for the sake of love...

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:55.050
First, she ended up with the Confederation...

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:55.920
As long as you can ignite the will to fight for the sake of love...

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.050
There are no doubts

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:03.800
The two of us together, we could even turn to evil

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:09.310
Spread your wings and take flight, twin bird

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:15.940
It's as if it's the beginning of the world

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:17.230
And then...

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:20.240
It's as if it's the beginning of the world

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:26.280
Into this empty body...

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:31.670
Memories are piling thick like snowfall

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:38.460
They are my guidepost to tomorrow

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:44.300
The tolls of the bell called loneliness beckon me into darkness

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:50.310
I focus on the moment as the time draws near

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:54.480
Soar high, O angel of sorrow...

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.020
And shed the past

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:01.320
You hold your head up high until the end of the cycle of life...

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.320
And go on surviving

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:09.200
Even if the whole world turns against you...

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.640
Fight as you were destined to, twin bird

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:13.440
And that's how she got caught in that loop...

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:17.130
Fight as you were destined to, twin bird

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:40.610
Bizon...

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:41.990
So, it was you.

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:44.700
Piloting that Valiancer...

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:47.660
I'll kill you...

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.240
I'll kill you all!

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:53.000
Who did that?!

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.830
Evgeni Kedar, you will cease hostilities at once.

00:12:57.480 --> 00:13:00.170
I am placing you under arrest on the charge of inciting civil strife.

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:01.170
What?

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:05.050
Political power seized though violent means is worthless.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:09.430
There were many who were equally displeased with the Administration Bureau's tyrannical ways.

00:13:10.090 --> 00:13:15.440
Things proceeded faster than I expected while you were up here in space.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:18.810
You went too far when you hit the Alaska Base.

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:21.320
Images of the casualties there served as the trigger.

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:29.280
You tightened the noose around your own neck,
former Chairman of the Provisional Supreme Council.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.950
This is being broadcast to the entire military.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.660
Could it be that we've been saved?

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:44.760
So what?!

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.340
This battlefield is under my control!

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:49.550
My control!

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:01.820
My revenge is not over yet!

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:05.650
My revenge, which I've held onto for 70 years!

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:07.320
Give it up already, Bizon!

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:08.740
Shut up!

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:13.830
I'll squash you here and now, Hina.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.790
It's your fault!

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:19.960
If you'd only quietly laid down beneath me!

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:33.720
I can understand a little of how you feel...
Watching Hina all this time...

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:38.230
Watase Aoba!

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:50.200
But what you wanted to protect was your own pride and ego!

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:56.450
But I... <i>We</i> have things we want to protect!

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:01.420
Are you all right, Hina?

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:02.250
Yes.

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:08.670
It's over.

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:29.610
A-Am I going to die?

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:31.740
If so...

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:39.960
Detecting a high energy reading from the enemy attack satellite!

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.210
It's still increasing!

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:47.710
There's three years' worth of Nectoribium stored in the satellite, and I've unleashed it all at once.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:48.710
This is crazy!

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:53.180
There's no way this satellite can withstand that kind of energy!

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:55.970
Damn it!

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:01.690
Don't screw with me!

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:04.980
I'm not meant to die in a place like this!

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:08.940
My brains and my research... It can't all end here!

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:11.650
This is my revenge.

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:23.330
It doesn't matter if we can't destroy the satellite!

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:25.500
It'll be enough if we can just shift it's line of fire.

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:31.210
A Nectar Curtain?!

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:33.720
The calculations are in for the enemy's targets.

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:39.470
Kumtor and Muruntau in the Republic of Zogilia,
and Kalgoorlie in Australia, a member state of the Confederation!

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:41.140
Th-Three locations?!

00:16:41.140 --> 00:16:43.480
But why attack his own country as well?

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:47.440
They're all the world's top production sites for Nectoribium.

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:51.070
There's said to be several decades worth of Nectoribium underground.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:55.240
If that's hit by a giant Nectar Cannon,
it'll cause secondary explosions on a massive scale.

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:57.820
What will happen then?

00:16:57.820 --> 00:17:00.620
Probably the complete destruction

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:01.870
of Earth.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.040
I won't let that happen!

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.000
We'll go take it down ourselves!

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:10.880
But the distance to the satellite...!

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:13.260
With the Coupling units, we might be able to make it!

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:14.010
But...!

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:15.510
No buts!

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:18.260
There's no way we'll know unless we try, right?

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.470
Yeah.

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.640
Here we go, Dio!

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:21.810
All right!

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:23.270
Aoba!

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:26.810
It's no use.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:28.690
There isn't enough time left now.

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:45.160
Not yet!
Not yet!

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:58.260
What was that just now?

00:17:58.260 --> 00:17:59.430
Hell if I know!

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:01.850
Don't worry about it, stopping that thing is our first priority!

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:03.560
Don't order me around!

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.560
Elvira-san, this is...

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:08.060
This is...

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:11.310
Aoba-kun and Dio are skipping through time?

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:12.570
What do you mean?
What?

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:14.530
To synchronize thoughts without any delay,

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:21.990
the Coupling System sends elementary particles as signals one nanosecond into the future.

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:27.870
If their thoughts were to be in such alignment as to not need that...

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:31.330
The signal would be sent from the zeroth second to the zeroth second...

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:36.130
But to make up for the phenomenon of
transmitting one nanosecond into the future...

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:40.640
It's sending both the receiver and the receiving machine one nanosecond back into the past?!

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:42.300
Is something like that really—

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:43.640
I don't know!

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:45.390
But that's the only thing I can...

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:51.560
Assuming that's true, in order to go back one nanosecond in time, Aoba and Dio are...

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:54.070
They're jumping a million times over?!

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:10.000
Travel distance has further increased!

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:13.960
Go!

00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:15.710
Go, Aoba!

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:18.630
Go!

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:19.840
Aoba-san!

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:21.550
Dio...

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:28.640
Aoba...

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:50.290
Aoba-san!

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:03.430
Singularity has appeared at Point E7-R1!

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:09.100
Aoba!

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.100
Don't, Dio!

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:12.940
You'll get sucked into it, too!

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:13.980
But...

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:16.110
Bradyon is already at its limit, right?

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:17.860
If anyone's going after them, it's us!

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:20.650
It's okay. Fromm. Dio.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:25.620
Dio, you saw it, so you know, right?

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:29.120
We're going to continue on, back to our own world.

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:31.750
But...!

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.830
You know...

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:40.760
Never in my wildest dreams did I think I'd become close
friends with someone from 70 years into the future.

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:44.260
Give my best to everyone else for me.

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:46.760
Thank them for everything they did for me.

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:49.260
If that's what you want, tell them yourself!

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:53.480
It doesn't look like I've got that kind of time left, so...

00:20:54.550 --> 00:20:56.020
Aoba-san...

00:20:56.770 --> 00:21:00.230
You... appeared out of the blue...

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:02.240
Got us all stirred up, and now...

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:04.240
Just as suddenly...

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:07.740
So long, Dio.

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:26.300
We've lost signal from the Luxon Next and the Karura.

00:21:41.050 --> 00:21:44.800
With my heart, I call out

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:49.180
To the far side, mutually drawn

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:53.690
Forgetting even the reason I ache

00:21:53.690 --> 00:21:58.310
Just for now, please

00:21:58.310 --> 00:22:02.490
I know you

00:22:02.490 --> 00:22:06.990
I'm searching for you

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:09.450
Softly pressing my lips

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:16.040
to the bright afterimage I can't keep from leaving

00:22:16.040 --> 00:22:24.590
If hesitation is what gives way to the slightest of hopes

00:22:24.590 --> 00:22:29.220
To the many gentle mornings...

00:22:29.220 --> 00:22:33.770
and the times I have wondered

00:22:33.770 --> 00:22:38.020
In the future that leads back to that sky,

00:22:38.020 --> 00:22:40.230
I want to save you,

00:22:40.230 --> 00:22:42.360
I want to protect you

00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:46.740
In the future that arrives at that dream

00:22:46.740 --> 00:22:49.620
Wait for me

00:22:49.620 --> 00:22:54.370
The love we'll surely find

00:22:54.370 --> 00:22:59.170
I want you to reach out for it

00:23:05.320 --> 00:23:07.030
Hina, hold up!

00:23:07.030 --> 00:23:08.820
You don't have to be in such a rush!

00:23:09.340 --> 00:23:12.490
But if we don't hurry, we'll be late for our next class.

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:15.870
Oh, sorry, you okay?

00:23:15.870 --> 00:23:17.910
Oh, no, I should be the one apologizing.

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:21.580
Have we met somewhere before?

00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:23.420
Whoa, Hina, you're hitting on him?

00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:24.420
I-I'm not...

00:23:24.420 --> 00:23:26.630
No, we've never met.

00:23:28.410 --> 00:23:30.340
I'm Watase Aoba.

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:31.050
You?

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.800
Y-Yumihara Hina.
